IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-nouns`
IMPORT `spr-part1-general`
IMPORT `spr-part2-prisoners`
IMPORT `spr-part3-deferral`
IMPORT `spr-part4-qualifying-years`
IMPORT `spr-part5-sharing`
IMPORT `spr-part6-graduated`
IMPORT `spr-part7-overseas`
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-general`
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-post2016`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), version 2026-04-06 (plain-text rendering; not the official text) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or will become, entitled to the State Pension, asking what these Regulations mean for when and how their
-- State Pension is claimed, paid and affected by their choices.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the spr- modules imported above as the questions that person would ask about their
-- own pension. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the records the modules expect from plain
-- answers, inside its WHERE, and then calls the module's own rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates, or the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the person
-- can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed
-- placeholder, with a comment saying so. Where the text makes the person's position depend on something on the other side -- a notice
-- the Secretary of State has or has not issued, a direction to use writing, a view that a late choice is reasonable, a certified release
-- date, a request for a declaration, whether Regulations apply regulation 21 -- that fact is a plain input too, voiced to the person
-- ("Has the Secretary of State told you ...?"); the judgment itself is never presumed.
--
-- FIGURES TAKEN AS THE TEXT STATES THEM: the full rate of the State Pension (£241.30 a week, regulation 1A, in the version of 6 April
-- 2026), the specified percentage (one-ninth of 1%, regulation 10), 6 April 2016 and the other dates and periods the text names. The person
-- cannot state those; if an amending instrument changes one, these answers change with it.
--
-- WHAT A PERSON CANNOT BE ASKED: a record of dates (a list of notices, a list of non-uprating changes) is asked as the most recent
-- notice, or the first and second change; the longer encoding takes any number (see NOTES.md).
--
-- Groups that arise only in a situation the person may not be in (custody; a choice between a lump sum and a pension; suspending or
-- deferring; a survivor's pension; living abroad; credits for a particular kind of week) carry that in the heading comment, so the form
-- can ask "Has this happened to you?" before showing them.

§ `State Pension Regulations 2015 -- the pensioner's questions`

§§ `Do these Regulations apply to me, and how are people counted? (Parts 1 and 1A)`

-- Regulation 1(3). The Regulations (except Part 5) do not apply to a person who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016: they are
-- for people who reach it on or after that day.
@export Do these Regulations apply to me (reg 1(3))?
GIVEN `the day I reach State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach State Pension age? (If you already have, the date you reached it.)
GIVETH A `Whether the Regulations apply to a person`
DECIDE `Do these Regulations apply to me` IS
    `whether Parts 1 to 4 and 6 to 8 apply to a person who reaches pensionable age on` `the day I reach State Pension age`

-- Regulation 1(5). Two people are treated as not married to each other for the times when either of them is married to a third person
-- (only the marriage is taken away; civil partners stay civil partners).
@export Does the law count the other person and me as married or civil partners for these Regulations (reg 1(5))?
GIVEN `how the other person and I are joined` IS A `How two people are joined` @desc Are you and the other person married to each other, civil partners of each other, or neither?
      `one of us is married to a third person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is either of you married to someone else?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the law count the other person and me as spouses or civil partners` IF
    `the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` `the two of us`
    WHERE
        `the two of us` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
            `how they are joined` IS `how the other person and I are joined`
            `either of them is married to a third person` IS `one of us is married to a third person`

-- Regulation 1A. The full rate of the State Pension, per week.
@export What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension, in pounds (reg 1A)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension` IS
    `the full rate of the state pension, in pounds per week`

§§ `Prison and other custody (Part 2) -- only if you are, or have been, in custody`

-- Regulations 2 and 3. The Secretary of State may withhold the State Pension for any day on which a person is a prisoner (imprisoned or
-- detained in legal custody in connection with criminal proceedings; unlawfully at large; or detained under certain mental health
-- Acts), except that a person remanded in custody is paid unless and until a sentence of imprisonment or detention is later imposed
-- for the offence. This is what the Secretary of State may do to you, so the questions below are about what you can be made to go
-- without, and the facts the answer depends on, including the release date the Secretary of State has certified.
@export Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody (regs 2, 3)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `the kind of custody I am in on that day` IS A `Kind of custody` @desc What kind of custody are you in on that day?
      `I am in Great Britain on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Great Britain on that day?
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would not have been a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are held outside Great Britain: in similar circumstances in Great Britain, would you not have been a prisoner?
      `the Secretary of State has certified my release date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983: has the Secretary of State certified a date for your release?
      `the release date certified` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is that date? (Any date if none.)
      `I was remanded in custody for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you remanded in custody for an offence?
      `a sentence has since been imposed for that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a sentence since been imposed for that offence?
      `the kind of sentence imposed` IS A `Kind of sentence` @desc If so, what kind of sentence was it? (Any if none.)
      `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that sentence imposed outside Great Britain?
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain it would not have been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was imposed outside Great Britain: in similar circumstances in Great Britain, would a sentence of imprisonment or detention not have been imposed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` IF
    `a state pension is not to be paid for the day` `my day in custody`
    WHERE
        `my day in custody` MEANS `A day of a person's custody` WITH
            `the day` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the kind of custody` IS `the kind of custody I am in on that day`
            `in Great Britain` IS `I am in Great Britain on that day`
            `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would not have been a prisoner`
            `the release date the Secretary of State has certified` IS
                IF `the Secretary of State has certified my release date` THEN JUST `the release date certified` ELSE NOTHING
            `remanded in custody for an offence` IS `I was remanded in custody for an offence`
            `the sentence later imposed for that offence` IS
                IF   `a sentence has since been imposed for that offence`
                THEN JUST (`Sentence imposed` WITH
                         `its kind` IS `the kind of sentence imposed`
                         `it was imposed outside Great Britain` IS `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain`
                         `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS `in similar circumstances in Great Britain it would not have been imposed`)
                ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Choosing a lump sum or a state pension (Part 3, regulations 4 to 6) -- only if you inherited a deferred state pension and have such a choice`

-- Regulation 4(1) to (3). A person within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act (who has inherited a deferred state pension and so has a choice
-- under section 8(2)) has three months starting on the date in the Secretary of State's most recent notice that confirms the choice. If the
-- person chooses before any such notice, the period starts on the later of the day they claimed a state pension and the day their spouse
-- or civil partner died, and ends on the day they choose. The notice is the Secretary of State's, so whether you were sent one, and its
-- date, are facts you state.
@export Am I within the time to make my choice of a lump sum or a state pension (reg 4(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `I have been sent a notice that says I may make my choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State sent you a notice that confirms you may choose between a lump sum and a state pension?
      `the date on the most recent such notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date on the most recent such notice? (Any date if none.)
      `the day I claimed a state pension` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you claim a state pension?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `the day I make or made my choice` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make, or did you make, your choice?
GIVETH A `Where a choice falls against its period`
DECIDE `Am I within the time to make my choice` IS
    `where the choice falls against its period` `my facts for the period`
    WHERE
        `my facts for the period` MEANS `Facts for the period for a choice` WITH
            `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice` IS
                IF `I have been sent a notice that says I may make my choice` THEN LIST `the date on the most recent such notice` ELSE EMPTY
            `the date the person claimed a state pension` IS `the day I claimed a state pension`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the date the choice was made` IS `the day I make or made my choice`

-- Regulation 4(4). A person may make a late choice, after the period, if the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular
-- case and any lump sum already paid has been repaid in full and in the currency it was paid in. What you owe, if you want to change
-- to a state pension late, is the repayment; what the Secretary of State decides is whether it is reasonable.
@export May I make a late choice (reg 4(4))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider it reasonable in your case for you to make a late choice?
      `I was paid a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been paid any amount by way of, or on account of, a lump sum?
      `I have repaid it in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have you repaid it to the Secretary of State in full?
      `I repaid it in the currency it was paid in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did you repay it in the currency in which it was originally paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a late choice` IF
    `a late choice may be made` `my late choice facts`
    WHERE
        `my late choice facts` MEANS `Facts for a late choice` WITH
            `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in my case`
            `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS `I was paid a lump sum`
            `it has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS `I have repaid it in full`
            `it has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `I repaid it in the currency it was paid in`

-- Regulation 4(5). If a person makes a late choice to be paid a state pension, the lump sum they would have been paid is reduced to nil.
@export How much lump sum will I be paid after my choice (reg 4(5))?
GIVEN `the lump sum I would be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What lump sum, in pounds, would you be paid?
      `my choice is a state pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your choice a state pension (rather than a lump sum)?
      `my choice is a late choice that is allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a late choice that the rules allow (see the question on late choices)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much lump sum will I be paid after my choice` IS
    `the lump sum to be paid after a choice, the amount being` `the lump sum I would be paid` `and the choice being` `my choice` `and it being a late choice under paragraph (4)` `my choice is a late choice that is allowed`
    WHERE
        `my choice` MEANS
            IF `my choice is a state pension` THEN `a state pension` ELSE `a lump sum`

-- Regulations 5(2) and 5(3). You must make your choice in writing to an office the Secretary of State has told you in writing accepts
-- choices, or by telephone to a number it has so specified; but where the Secretary of State directs that the written manner must be
-- used, only writing will do. (Regulation 7(2) and (3) say the same about a notice to suspend, and regulation 18(3) takes it over
-- for a survivor's choice.)
@export Am I making my choice in a way the Regulations allow (regs 5(2), 5(3))?
GIVEN `how I make my choice` IS A `Manner of giving` @desc How do you make your choice: in writing, by telephone, or some other way?
      `the office or number was specified to me in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State told you in writing that the office or telephone number you use accepts choices?
      `I have been told I must use writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that you must make your choice in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I making my choice in a way the Regulations allow` IF
    `it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` `how I give it`
    WHERE
        `how I give it` MEANS `How something was given` WITH
            `the manner` IS `how I make my choice`
            `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it` IS `the office or number was specified to me in writing`
            `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used` IS `I have been told I must use writing`

-- Regulation 6. Having made your choice, you may change it once, within three months of the Secretary of State's notification of it (or a longer
-- period the Secretary of State considers reasonable), if you apply in a way the Regulations allow; to change to a state pension, any lump sum
-- already paid must have been repaid in full, in time and in the currency paid; to change to a lump sum, the state pension already paid
-- must be less than the lump sum. What you owe is the application and the repayment; the Secretary of State's side is the notification
-- date, any longer period and any direction to use writing.
@export May I change my choice (reg 6)?
GIVEN `I am applying to change my choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying to change your choice?
      `the date on the notification of my choice` IS A DATE @desc What is the date in the Secretary of State's notification that confirms the choice you made?
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you apply to change your choice?
      `the Secretary of State considers a longer period reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you apply after the first three months: does the Secretary of State consider a longer period reasonable in your case?
      `how I apply` IS A `Manner of giving` @desc How do you apply: in writing, by telephone, or some other way?
      `the office or number for my application was specified to me in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State told you in writing that the office or telephone number you use accepts applications?
      `I have been told to apply in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that you must apply in writing?
      `the choice I made` IS A `Payment chosen` @desc What did you choose: a lump sum or a state pension?
      `the choice I want instead` IS A `Payment chosen` @desc What do you want to change it to?
      `I was paid a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been paid any amount by way of, or on account of, a lump sum?
      `I have repaid it in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have you repaid it to the Secretary of State in full?
      `I repaid it in the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did you repay it within the period in which you may apply (three months, or the longer period)?
      `I repaid it in the currency it was paid in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did you repay it in the currency in which it was originally paid?
      `the state pension I have been paid so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How much state pension, in pounds, have you been paid so far for the deferral this choice is about?
      `the lump sum I would be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much lump sum, in pounds, would you be paid?
      `I have already changed this choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already changed a choice about this same deferral?
      `my choice was treated as made on a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your choice treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987 (payments on death)?
      `the person who made the choice has since died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who made the choice since died? (If you made the choice yourself and are asking for yourself, no.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I change my choice` IF
    `the choice may be altered` `my application`
    WHERE
        `my application` MEANS `Application to alter a choice` WITH
            `the person who made the choice has not subsequently died` IS (NOT `the person who made the choice has since died`)
            `an application is made to alter the choice` IS `I am applying to change my choice`
            `the date in the notification confirming the choice that has been made` IS `the date on the notification of my choice`
            `the date the application is made` IS `the date I apply`
            `the application is made within a longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS `the Secretary of State considers a longer period reasonable`
            `how the application is made` IS `How something was given` WITH
                `the manner` IS `how I apply`
                `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it` IS `the office or number for my application was specified to me in writing`
                `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used` IS `I have been told to apply in writing`
            `the choice that has been made` IS `the choice I made`
            `the choice the application would substitute` IS `the choice I want instead`
            `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS `I was paid a lump sum`
            `it has been repaid in full` IS `I have repaid it in full`
            `it was repaid within the period in paragraph (2)(c)` IS `I repaid it in the time allowed`
            `it was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `I repaid it in the currency it was paid in`
            `the amount paid by way of a state pension` IS `the state pension I have been paid so far`
            `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum` IS `the lump sum I would be paid`
            `an alteration has already been made in respect of the same deferral` IS `I have already changed this choice`
            `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987` IS `my choice was treated as made on a death`

-- Regulation 6(3). Where you change to a lump sum, the state pension already paid for the deferral is treated as paid on account of
-- the lump sum, so only the difference is still to be paid.
@export How much of my lump sum is still to be paid if I change to a lump sum (reg 6(3))?
GIVEN `the lump sum I would be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much lump sum, in pounds, would you be paid?
      `the state pension I have been paid so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How much state pension, in pounds, have you been paid so far for that deferral?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my lump sum is still to be paid` IS
    `the part of the lump sum still to be paid, the lump sum being` `the lump sum I would be paid` `and the state pension already paid being` `the state pension I have been paid so far`

§§ `Suspending or deferring my State Pension (Part 3, regulations 7 to 12A) -- only if you have suspended, or are deferring, your State Pension`

-- Regulation 7. A person who has become entitled to a state pension may opt to suspend it by giving notice to the Secretary of State, in
-- writing to an office, or by telephone to a number, that the Secretary of State has specified to them in writing; if the Secretary of State
-- directs that writing must be used, only writing will do.
@export Does my notice suspend my State Pension (reg 7)?
GIVEN `I have become entitled to a state pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014?
      `I have given notice that I opt to suspend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice to the Secretary of State that you opt to suspend your entitlement?
      `how I gave my notice` IS A `Manner of giving` @desc How did you give your notice: in writing, by telephone, or some other way?
      `the office or number for my notice was specified to me in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State told you in writing that the office or telephone number you used accepts such notices?
      `I have been told to give notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that you must give notice in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my notice suspend my State Pension` IF
    `entitlement is suspended by a notice` `my notice`
    WHERE
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice suspending entitlement` WITH
            `the person has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS `I have become entitled to a state pension`
            `the person has given notice to the Secretary of State` IS `I have given notice that I opt to suspend it`
            `how the notice was given` IS `How something was given` WITH
                `the manner` IS `how I gave my notice`
                `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it` IS `the office or number for my notice was specified to me in writing`
                `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used` IS `I have been told to give notice in writing`

-- Regulation 8. The suspension takes effect from a date you specify that is not before the day you exercised your option and not after 28
-- days starting with that day; if you do not specify one in that range, from the day you exercised your option.
@export From what date does my suspension take effect (reg 8)?
GIVEN `the day I exercised my option to suspend` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you exercise your option to suspend your State Pension?
      `I named a date for the suspension to start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you name a date from which the suspension is to take effect?
      `the date I named` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date did you name? (Any date if none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what date does my suspension take effect` IS
    `the date from which the suspension takes effect` `my suspension facts`
    WHERE
        `my suspension facts` MEANS `Facts for the start of a suspension` WITH
            `the date on which the option was exercised` IS `the day I exercised my option to suspend`
            `the date the person specifies` IS
                IF `I named a date for the suspension to start` THEN JUST `the date I named` ELSE NOTHING

-- Regulation 9. A person who has suspended may cancel the suspension for the whole or part of a past period of up to 12 months before
-- the day they cancel, by claiming their state pension while it is suspended.
@export May I cancel my suspension for a past period (reg 9)?
GIVEN `I opted to suspend my State Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you opt to suspend your State Pension?
      `I claimed my State Pension while it was suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a claim for your State Pension while it was suspended?
      `the day I cancel the suspension` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you cancel the suspension (the date of your claim)?
      `the first day of the period I want cancelled` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the past period you want the suspension cancelled for?
      `the last day of the period I want cancelled` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that past period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I cancel my suspension for a past period` IF
    `the suspension is cancelled for the past period` `my cancellation facts`
    WHERE
        `my cancellation facts` MEANS `Facts for cancelling a suspension` WITH
            `the person opted to suspend entitlement` IS `I opted to suspend my State Pension`
            `the person made a claim for a state pension whilst it was suspended` IS `I claimed my State Pension while it was suspended`
            `the date on which the person cancels the suspension` IS `the day I cancel the suspension`
            `the first day of the past period` IS `the first day of the period I want cancelled`
            `the last day of the past period` IS `the last day of the period I want cancelled`

-- Regulation 10. The percentage of the weekly rate that each whole week of deferral earns: one-ninth of 1%.
@export What percentage of my weekly pension does each whole week of deferral add (reg 10)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What percentage of my weekly pension does each whole week of deferral add` IS
    `the specified percentage for the increase in the weekly rate`

-- Regulations 10 and 12A(2). The increment for each whole week is that percentage of the weekly rate you would have been paid had you
-- not deferred (immediately before the end of the stretch of deferral it belongs to).
@export How much does each whole week of my deferral add to my weekly pension, in pounds (regs 10, 12A(2))?
GIVEN `the weekly rate I would have been paid had I not deferred` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate of State Pension, in pounds, would you have been paid immediately before the end of the stretch of deferral, had you not deferred?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does each whole week of my deferral add to my weekly pension` IS
    `the increment for each whole week of a modification period, the weekly rate being` `the weekly rate I would have been paid had I not deferred`

-- Regulation 11. A day does not count towards your weeks of deferral if you received one of the listed benefits that day, or someone
-- received an increase of one in respect of you and is married to, in a civil partnership with, or living with you, or you would not have
-- been paid your State Pension that day had you not deferred because you were a prisoner.
@export Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted (reg 11)?
GIVEN `the benefit I received on that day` IS A `Benefit that stops a day counting` @desc Which of these benefits did you receive on that day (or none of them)?
      `someone received an increase of one of those benefits for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did someone receive an increase of one of those benefits in respect of you on that day?
      `how that person and I are joined` IS A `How two people are joined` @desc If so, are that person and you married to each other, civil partners of each other, or neither?
      `that person or I am married to a third person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is either of you married to someone else?
      `that person and I live together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, do that person and you live together?
      `the kind of custody I was in that day` IS A `Kind of custody` @desc What kind of custody were you in that day (or none)?
      `I was in Great Britain that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in Great Britain that day?
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would not have been a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If held outside Great Britain: in similar circumstances in Great Britain, would you not have been a prisoner?
      `the Secretary of State has certified my release date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983: has the Secretary of State certified a release date?
      `the release date certified` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is that date? (Any date if none.)
      `I was remanded in custody for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you remanded in custody for an offence?
      `a sentence has since been imposed for that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a sentence since been imposed for that offence?
      `the kind of sentence imposed` IS A `Kind of sentence` @desc If so, what kind of sentence? (Any if none.)
      `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that sentence imposed outside Great Britain?
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain it would not have been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: in similar circumstances in Great Britain, would a sentence of imprisonment or detention not have been imposed?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` IF
    `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` `my day of deferral`
    WHERE
        `my day of deferral` MEANS `A day of the deferral period` WITH
            `the benefit the person received on the day` IS `the benefit I received on that day`
            `an increase of one of those benefits was received in respect of the person on the day` IS `someone received an increase of one of those benefits for me`
            `the person who received the increase and the person whose entitlement is deferred` IS `Two people at a time` WITH
                `how they are joined` IS `how that person and I are joined`
                `either of them is married to a third person` IS `that person or I am married to a third person`
            `they reside together` IS `that person and I live together`
            `the person's custody on the day` IS `A day of a person's custody` WITH
                `the day` IS `the day I am asking about`
                `the kind of custody` IS `the kind of custody I was in that day`
                `in Great Britain` IS `I was in Great Britain that day`
                `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would not have been a prisoner`
                `the release date the Secretary of State has certified` IS
                    IF `the Secretary of State has certified my release date` THEN JUST `the release date certified` ELSE NOTHING
                `remanded in custody for an offence` IS `I was remanded in custody for an offence`
                `the sentence later imposed for that offence` IS
                    IF   `a sentence has since been imposed for that offence`
                    THEN JUST (`Sentence imposed` WITH
                             `its kind` IS `the kind of sentence imposed`
                             `it was imposed outside Great Britain` IS `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain`
                             `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS `in similar circumstances in Great Britain it would not have been imposed`)
                    ELSE NOTHING

-- Regulation 12. After the days left out under regulation 11 are taken off, any part of a week in the total period of deferral is
-- treated as a whole week.
@export How many whole weeks of deferral do I have (reg 12)?
GIVEN `the first day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your period of deferral?
      `the last day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your period of deferral?
      `the days of it that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of that period do not count under regulation 11?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many whole weeks of deferral do I have` IS
    `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` (`the number of days in the deferral period` `my deferral period`) `days, of which` `the days of it that do not count` `do not count`
    WHERE
        `my deferral period` MEANS `Deferral period` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of my deferral`
            `last day` IS `the last day of my deferral`

-- Regulation 12A. If, during your deferral, the weekly rate you would have been paid changed for a reason other than an up-rating, the
-- deferral is divided into modification periods at each such change, and the increment is worked out for each. Up to two changes are asked.
@export Into how many stretches is my deferral divided if my weekly rate changed other than by up-rating (reg 12A)?
GIVEN `the first day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your period of deferral?
      `the last day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your period of deferral?
      `my weekly rate changed once` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the weekly rate you would have been paid change, other than by an up-rating increase, during your deferral?
      `the day of the first such change` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did the first such change take effect? (Any date if none.)
      `my weekly rate changed a second time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it change again, other than by up-rating?
      `the day of the second such change` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Into how many stretches is my deferral divided` IS
    count (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `my deferral period` `given the non-uprating changes` `my changes`)
    WHERE
        `my deferral period` MEANS `Deferral period` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of my deferral`
            `last day` IS `the last day of my deferral`
        `my changes` MEANS
            IF   `my weekly rate changed once`
            THEN IF   `my weekly rate changed a second time`
                 THEN LIST `the day of the first such change`, `the day of the second such change`
                 ELSE LIST `the day of the first such change`
            ELSE EMPTY

§§ `How many qualifying years I need (Part 4)`

-- Regulation 13(1). The minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the reduced rate is ten. (A qualifying year is
-- the 2014 Act's: a tax year for which you have paid or been credited enough; you state how many you have.)
@export Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the reduced rate (reg 13(1))?
GIVEN `the number of qualifying years I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying years do you have?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the reduced rate` IF
    `the person has the minimum number of qualifying years for the reduced rate` `the number of qualifying years I have`

-- Regulation 13(2). The same minimum, ten, applies for a state pension at the transitional rate.
@export Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the transitional rate (reg 13(2))?
GIVEN `the number of qualifying years I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying years do you have?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the transitional rate` IF
    `the person has the minimum number of qualifying years for the transitional rate` `the number of qualifying years I have`

§§ `Sharing State Pension rights on divorce or dissolution (Part 5 and the Schedule) -- only if a court is dividing pension rights or you have asked about it`

-- The Schedule, paragraph 1(10), inserted regulation 6(1) to (6). When you ask the Secretary of State for information about shareable new state
-- scheme rights (or a court order or provision calls for it), the Secretary of State must give you a valuation as at the right date, and always
-- an explanation. This lists what you are owed.
@export What information must the Secretary of State give me when I ask about sharing my State Pension rights (Schedule, inserted reg 6(1) to (6))?
GIVEN `the day the Secretary of State receives my request or the order` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Secretary of State receive your request or the court order?
      `there is a relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a "relevant date" (the date under section 10(3) of the Family Law (Scotland) Act 1985)?
      `my relevant date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is it? (Any date if none.)
      `my request or the order includes a valuation or an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request or the order ask for a valuation, or for the amount of a former category A retirement pension entitlement?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Item of information about sharing`
DECIDE `What information must the Secretary of State give me when I ask about sharing my State Pension rights` IS
    `the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` `my request`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `Request for information about sharing` WITH
            `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the order` IS `the day the Secretary of State receives my request or the order`
            `the relevant date` IS
                IF `there is a relevant date` THEN JUST `my relevant date` ELSE NOTHING
            `the request or order includes a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)` IS `my request or the order includes a valuation or an amount`
            -- Placeholder: the information rule does not read this field.
            `the person notified the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed in connection with proceedings` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the information rule does not read this field.
            `the last day of a shorter period specified by the court in an order` IS NOTHING

-- Schedule, inserted regulation 6(1)(b). Your spouse or civil partner is owed the explanation in paragraph (6).
@export What information must the Secretary of State give my spouse or civil partner (Schedule, inserted reg 6(1)(b))?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Item of information about sharing`
DECIDE `What information must the Secretary of State give my spouse or civil partner` IS
    `the information the spouse or civil partner of the person is owed on request`

-- The Schedule, inserted regulation 6(7) and (8). By when the Secretary of State must give it: within three months beginning with the day
-- the request or order is received, or six weeks if you have told the Secretary of State by then that it is needed in connection with
-- proceedings, or any shorter period the court specifies; where no valuation or amount is asked for, within one month.
@export By what date must the Secretary of State give me that information (Schedule, inserted reg 6(7), (8))?
GIVEN `the day the Secretary of State receives my request or the order` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Secretary of State receive your request or the court order?
      `my request or the order includes a valuation or an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request or the order ask for a valuation, or for the amount of a former category A retirement pension entitlement?
      `I told the Secretary of State it is needed for proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed in connection with proceedings?
      `the court set a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court specified a shorter period in an order?
      `the last day of the court's period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that period? (Any date if none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must the Secretary of State give me that information` IS
    `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` `my request`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `Request for information about sharing` WITH
            `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the order` IS `the day the Secretary of State receives my request or the order`
            -- Placeholder: the deadline rule does not read this field.
            `the relevant date` IS NOTHING
            `the request or order includes a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)` IS `my request or the order includes a valuation or an amount`
            `the person notified the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed in connection with proceedings` IS `I told the Secretary of State it is needed for proceedings`
            `the last day of a shorter period specified by the court in an order` IS
                IF `the court set a shorter period` THEN JUST `the last day of the court's period` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `A survivor's state pension from a late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit (Part 6) -- only if your spouse or civil partner has died`

-- Regulation 15(1) and (2). You are entitled if your dead spouse or civil partner paid graduated contributions as an insured person; you have reached
-- pensionable age; they died while you were married or civil partners; the marriage or civil partnership began before 6 April 2016; and you are entitled to an
-- inherited amount under regulation 16(1), (2) or (3).
@export Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit (reg 15)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `my spouse or civil partner paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your late spouse or civil partner pay graduated contributions as an insured person?
      `we were married or civil partners when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to each other, or civil partners of each other, when they died?
      `the day we married or formed our civil partnership` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you marry, or form your civil partnership?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner reach State Pension age before they died?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `the day I reach or reached State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `I have married or formed a civil partnership since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the death, and before you reached State Pension age, have you married or formed a civil partnership?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` IF
    `a state pension is payable under regulation 15` `me as a survivor`
    WHERE
        `me as a survivor` MEANS `Facts about a survivor` WITH
            `the date as at which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS `my spouse or civil partner paid graduated contributions as an insured person`
            `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS `we were married or civil partners when they died`
            `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS `the day we married or formed our civil partnership`
            `the date the deceased died` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS IF `my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` THEN JUST `the day my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` ELSE NOTHING
            `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS `the day I reach or reached State Pension age`
            `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS `I have married or formed a civil partnership since`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE

-- Regulation 15(3). The pension is payable at a weekly rate equal to the inherited amount; NOTHING if it is not payable to you.
