GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `my spouse or civil partner paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your late spouse or civil partner pay graduated contributions as an insured person?
      `we were married or civil partners when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to each other, or civil partners of each other, when they died?
      `the day we married or formed our civil partnership` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you marry, or form your civil partnership?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner reach State Pension age before they died?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `the day I reach or reached State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `I have married or formed a civil partnership since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the death, and before you reached State Pension age, have you married or formed a civil partnership?
      `the weekly rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate, in pounds, of your late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit, worked out as regulation 16(5) says (up-rating orders since the death treated as in force before it, and leaving out additions under section 36(4) or 37(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly rate will my state pension under regulation 15 be` IS
    `the weekly rate of a state pension under regulation 15` `me as a survivor` `the weekly rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit`
    WHERE
        `me as a survivor` MEANS `Facts about a survivor` WITH
            `the date as at which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS `my spouse or civil partner paid graduated contributions as an insured person`
            `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS `we were married or civil partners when they died`
            `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS `the day we married or formed our civil partnership`
            `the date the deceased died` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS IF `my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` THEN JUST `the day my spouse or civil partner reached State Pension age` ELSE NOTHING
            `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS `the day I reach or reached State Pension age`
            `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS `I have married or formed a civil partnership since`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE

