-- Regulation 17. Your pension under regulation 15 rises with the full rate if, with your other state pensions, it does not exceed the full rate (paragraphs (3), (4));
-- by a percentage of the shortfall or the excess if it takes the total over the full rate while your other pensions are below it (paragraphs (5) to (7)); and by the
-- uprating order's percentage if your other pensions alone reach the full rate (paragraphs (8), (9)). The full rate and the uprating order are the State's side.
@export By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise, in pounds a week (reg 17)?
GIVEN `my pension under regulation 15, in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate, in pounds, is your state pension under regulation 15 (before any section 17 increase, and as regulation 17(2) describes it)?
      `my other state pensions, in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total weekly rate, in pounds, of any state pension you are entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the Pensions Act 2014?
      `the full rate before the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension, in pounds, immediately before the increase?
      `the full rate is increased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the full rate of the State Pension being increased?
      `the full rate after the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what will it be, in pounds a week? (Any amount if not.)
      `an uprating order comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an uprating order under section 151A of the Administration Act coming into force?
      `the percentage in the uprating order` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage does it specify, as a fraction (4% is 0.04)? (Any number if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` IS
    `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` `my up-rating facts`
    WHERE
        `my up-rating facts` MEANS `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension` WITH
            `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15` IS `my pension under regulation 15, in pounds a week`
            `the sum of the rates of any state pension the person is entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act` IS `my other state pensions, in pounds a week`
            `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase` IS `the full rate before the increase`
            `the full rate of the state pension after an increase, if the full rate is increased` IS
                IF `the full rate is increased` THEN JUST `the full rate after the increase` ELSE NOTHING
            `the percentage specified in an uprating order, if one comes into force` IS
                IF `an uprating order comes into force` THEN JUST `the percentage in the uprating order` ELSE NOTHING

-- Regulation 18(1) and (8). You are entitled to a choice between a lump sum and a state pension if you have reached pensionable age; your spouse or civil partner died
-- while you were married or civil partners; their graduated retirement benefit was deferred at death and for the 12 months before; and either you were under pensionable
-- age then and have not remarried, or you were over it; but not if you are entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the Pensions Act 2014.
@export Am I entitled to a choice between a lump sum and a state pension (reg 18(1), (8))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `we were married or civil partners when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to each other, or civil partners of each other, when they died?
      `their graduated retirement benefit was deferred at death and for the 12 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit deferred when they died and throughout the 12 months ending the day before?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `the day I reach or reached State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `I have married or formed a civil partnership since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the death, and before you reached State Pension age, have you married or formed a civil partnership?
      `I am entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the Pensions Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a choice between a lump sum and a state pension under section 8(2) of the Pensions Act 2014?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a choice between a lump sum and a state pension` IF
    `the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` `me as a survivor`
    WHERE
        `me as a survivor` MEANS `Facts about a survivor` WITH
            `the date as at which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS TRUE
            `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS `we were married or civil partners when they died`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the date the deceased died` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS NOTHING
            `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS `the day I reach or reached State Pension age`
            `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS `I have married or formed a civil partnership since`
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS `their graduated retirement benefit was deferred at death and for the 12 months before`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
            `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS `I am entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the Pensions Act 2014`

-- Regulation 18(2) to (6), (9) to (11). What you are paid depends on the choice you made and how: a choice in time is paid as chosen; a late choice is paid as chosen if allowed
-- (the Secretary of State considers it reasonable and any lump sum has been repaid in full and in the currency), and otherwise you stay with the lump sum; no choice, or one
-- not made in the manner of regulation 5(2) and (3), leads to a lump sum once the period for choosing has ended. Whether the period has ended without a choice, and the
-- notice and its date, are the Secretary of State's side and are stated by you.
@export What am I paid after my choice (reg 18)?
GIVEN `I have made a choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a choice between a lump sum and a state pension?
      `what I chose` IS A `Payment chosen` @desc If so, what did you choose? (Either if none.)
      `how I made my choice` IS A `Manner of giving` @desc How did you make it: in writing, by telephone, or some other way? (Any if none.)
      `the office or number was specified to me in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the Secretary of State told you in writing that the office or telephone number you used accepts choices?
      `I was told to use writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the Secretary of State directed that you must make your choice in writing?
      `I have been sent a notice that says I may make my choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State sent you a notice that confirms you may make the choice?
      `the date on the most recent such notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date on the most recent such notice? (Any date if none.)
      `the day I claimed a state pension` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you claim a state pension?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `the day I made my choice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your choice? (Any date if none.)
      `the Secretary of State considers a late choice reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your choice was late: does the Secretary of State consider it reasonable in your case?
      `I was paid a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been paid any amount by way of, or on account of, a lump sum?
      `I have repaid it in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have you repaid it to the Secretary of State in full?
      `I repaid it in the currency it was paid in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did you repay it in the currency in which it was originally paid?
      `the period for choosing has ended without my choosing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the period for making your choice ended without you making one?
GIVETH A `What is paid under regulation 18`
DECIDE `What am I paid after my choice` IS
    `what is paid under regulation 18` `my facts for the payment`
    WHERE
        `my facts for the payment` MEANS `Facts for the payment under regulation 18` WITH
            `the choice the person made, if any` IS
                IF   `I have made a choice`
                THEN JUST (`A choice made under regulation 18` WITH
                         `the payment chosen` IS `what I chose`
                         `how the choice was made` IS `How something was given` WITH
                             `the manner` IS `how I made my choice`
                             `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it` IS `the office or number was specified to me in writing`
                             `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used` IS `I was told to use writing`
                         `the facts for the period` IS `Facts for the period for a choice` WITH
                             `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice` IS
                                 IF `I have been sent a notice that says I may make my choice` THEN LIST `the date on the most recent such notice` ELSE EMPTY
                             `the date the person claimed a state pension` IS `the day I claimed a state pension`
                             `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
                             `the date the choice was made` IS `the day I made my choice`
                         `the facts for a late choice` IS `Facts for a late choice` WITH
                             `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS `the Secretary of State considers a late choice reasonable`
                             `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS `I was paid a lump sum`
                             `it has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS `I have repaid it in full`
                             `it has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `I repaid it in the currency it was paid in`)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `the period for making a choice has ended without one being made` IS `the period for choosing has ended without my choosing`

-- Regulation 19(2). The date the dates in the 2005 Regulations are read as is the day you became entitled to make the choice: once you have reached pensionable age and
-- your spouse or civil partner has died, the later of the two.
@export From what date was I entitled to make my choice (reg 19(2))?
GIVEN `the day my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `the day I reach or reached State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what date was I entitled to make my choice` IS
    `the date the person becomes entitled to make a choice under regulation 18` `me as a survivor`
    WHERE
        `me as a survivor` MEANS `Facts about a survivor` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the date as at which the question is asked` IS `the day I reach or reached State Pension age`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the date the deceased died` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS NOTHING
            `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS `the day I reach or reached State Pension age`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE

-- Regulation 19(1). The lump sum is the amount worked out under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005
-- (which you state); you are paid it only if the outcome under regulation 18 is a lump sum.
@export How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19 (reg 19(1))?
GIVEN `the amount worked out under the 2005 Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What lump sum, in pounds, is worked out under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005?
      `what I am paid under regulation 18` IS A `What is paid under regulation 18` @desc What are you to be paid under regulation 18 (see the question "What am I paid after my choice")?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19` IS
    `the lump sum payable under regulation 19` `the amount worked out under the 2005 Regulations` `given` `what I am paid under regulation 18`

-- Regulation 20(1). You are entitled to a state pension under this regulation if you have reached pensionable age; your spouse or civil partner died while you were married or
-- civil partners; you were under pensionable age then and have not remarried, or over it; they were entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit or it was deferred
-- when they died; and, if you have a choice under regulation 18 (or would but for regulation 18(8)), you are to be paid a state pension under it. The last is the outcome you state.
@export Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's deferred graduated retirement benefit (reg 20(1))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `we were married or civil partners when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to each other, or civil partners of each other, when they died?
      `their graduated retirement benefit was deferred at death and for the 12 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit deferred when they died and throughout the 12 months ending the day before?
      `the day my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `the day I reach or reached State Pension age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `I have married or formed a civil partnership since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the death, and before you reached State Pension age, have you married or formed a civil partnership?
      `they were entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late spouse or civil partner entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit?
      `their graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was their entitlement to graduated retirement benefit deferred when they died?
      `what I am paid under regulation 18` IS A `What is paid under regulation 18` @desc What are you to be paid under regulation 18 (see the question "What am I paid after my choice")? If you have no choice under regulation 18, give any answer.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's deferred graduated retirement benefit` IF
    `a state pension is payable under regulation 20` `me as a survivor` `given` `what I am paid under regulation 18`
    WHERE
        `me as a survivor` MEANS `Facts about a survivor` WITH
            `the date as at which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS TRUE
            `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS `we were married or civil partners when they died`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the date the deceased died` IS `the day my spouse or civil partner died`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS NOTHING
            `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS `the day I reach or reached State Pension age`
            `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS `I have married or formed a civil partnership since`
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS `their graduated retirement benefit was deferred at death and for the 12 months before`
            `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS `they were entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit`
            `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS `their graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE

-- Regulation 20(2), (4), (5). The pension is half the weekly rate of your late spouse's or civil partner's increase in graduated retirement benefit (or the increase that would have been
-- payable had their deferral ended just before the death), determined as if up-rating orders between the death and your reaching pensionable age had been in force before the death
-- and without any addition under section 37(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965.
@export What weekly rate will my state pension under regulation 20 be, in pounds (reg 20(2))?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of their increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate, in pounds, of your late spouse's or civil partner's increase in graduated retirement benefit, worked out as regulation 20(4) says?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly rate will my state pension under regulation 20 be` IS
    `the weekly rate of a state pension under regulation 20` `the weekly rate of their increase in graduated retirement benefit`

-- Regulation 20(3). When an order under section 151A of the Administration Act comes into force, your pension under this regulation rises, from that time, by the
-- percentage the order specifies.
@export What will my state pension under regulation 20 be after an uprating order, in pounds a week (reg 20(3))?
GIVEN `my pension under regulation 20, in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate, in pounds, is your state pension under regulation 20 now?
      `the percentage in the uprating order` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage does the uprating order specify, as a fraction (4% is 0.04)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What will my state pension under regulation 20 be after an uprating order` IS
    `the rate of a state pension under regulation 20 after an uprating order` `my pension under regulation 20, in pounds a week` `and the percentage specified in the order being` `the percentage in the uprating order`

§§ `Living abroad (Part 7) -- only if you are, or have been, an overseas resident`

-- Regulation 21(1) to (5). An overseas resident entitled to a state pension is not entitled to up-rating increases, but only for an increase to which Regulations made under
-- regulation 21(2) apply it. If you deferred and, when the deferral ended, were entitled and an overseas resident, you lose increases in respect of the deferral period if you were
-- an overseas resident at the time and stayed one until it ended, and increases after it if you are an overseas resident at the time. In all other cases you lose an increase if,
-- immediately before it, you were entitled and an overseas resident. Whether Regulations apply regulation 21 to the increase is the State's side, and you state it.
@export Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad (reg 21)?
GIVEN `Regulations apply regulation 21 to this increase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have Regulations been made providing that regulation 21 applies to this up-rating increase?
      `my entitlement to a state pension had been deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your entitlement to a state pension deferred for a period?
      `when my deferral ended I was entitled to a state pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, when the deferral ended, were you entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014?
      `when my deferral ended I was an overseas resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, were you then an overseas resident?
      `where this increase falls against my deferral` IS A `When an up-rating increase falls against the deferral period` @desc Is the increase in respect of the deferral period, after it ended, or at some other time?
      `I was an overseas resident at the time of the increase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an overseas resident at the time of the increase (immediately before it came into force)?
      `I stayed an overseas resident until my deferral ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the increase is in respect of the deferral period: did you continue to be an overseas resident until the deferral ended?
      `I was entitled to a state pension just before the increase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 immediately before the increase?
GIVETH A `What regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase`
DECIDE `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` IS
    `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` `my increase facts`
    WHERE
        `my increase facts` MEANS `Facts about an up-rating increase for a person abroad` WITH
            `Regulations have been made providing that regulation 21 applies to the up-rating increase` IS `Regulations apply regulation 21 to this increase`
            `the person's entitlement to a state pension had been deferred for a period` IS `my entitlement to a state pension had been deferred`
            `when the deferral period ended the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS `when my deferral ended I was entitled to a state pension`
            `when the deferral period ended the person was an overseas resident` IS `when my deferral ended I was an overseas resident`
            `where the increase falls against the deferral period` IS `where this increase falls against my deferral`
            `the person was an overseas resident at the time of the increase` IS `I was an overseas resident at the time of the increase`
            `the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended` IS `I stayed an overseas resident until my deferral ended`
            `the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act immediately before the increase` IS `I was entitled to a state pension just before the increase`

-- Regulation 21(6). The territory specified is any part of the Channel Islands that is not subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act.
@export Is where I live a territory specified in regulation 21(6)?
GIVEN `I live in a part of the Channel Islands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live in a part of the Channel Islands?
      `that part is subject to an Order under section 179` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that part subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is where I live a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` IF
    `the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` `I live in a part of the Channel Islands` `given` `that part is subject to an Order under section 179`

-- Regulation 22(2) and (3). For a part of your deferral during which you were an overseas resident and not in Great Britain or a specified territory, your increment is a percentage of the
-- weekly rate immediately before the start of that part; for a part during which you were not an overseas resident, of the rate immediately before its end. A part during which you were an
-- overseas resident in Great Britain or a specified territory is in neither paragraph.
@export Which weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral (reg 22(2), (3))?
GIVEN `I was an overseas resident during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an overseas resident during that part of your deferral?
      `I was in Great Britain during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in Great Britain during that part?
      `I was in a part of the Channel Islands during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a part of the Channel Islands during that part?
      `that part is subject to an Order under section 179` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was that part subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act?
GIVETH A `Which weekly rate an increment is a percentage of`
DECIDE `Which weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` IS
    `which weekly rate the increment for a part is a percentage of` `that part of my deferral`
    WHERE
        `that part of my deferral` MEANS `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the first day of the part` IS Date 6 4 2016
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the last day of the part` IS Date 6 4 2016
            `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS `I was an overseas resident during that part`
            `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS
                `I was in Great Britain during that part` OR `the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` `I was in a part of the Channel Islands during that part` `given` `that part is subject to an Order under section 179`

@export What weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral, in pounds (reg 22(2), (3))?
GIVEN `I was an overseas resident during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an overseas resident during that part of your deferral?
      `I was in Great Britain during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in Great Britain during that part?
      `I was in a part of the Channel Islands during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a part of the Channel Islands during that part?
      `that part is subject to an Order under section 179` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was that part subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act?
      `my weekly rate just before the part began` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate of State Pension, in pounds, would you have been paid immediately before the start of that part, had you not deferred?
      `my weekly rate just before the part ended` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate would you have been paid immediately before the end of that part, had you not deferred?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` IS
    `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to for a part` `that part of my deferral` `given the rate at the start` `my weekly rate just before the part began` `and the rate at the end` `my weekly rate just before the part ended`
    WHERE
        `that part of my deferral` MEANS `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the first day of the part` IS Date 6 4 2016
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the last day of the part` IS Date 6 4 2016
            `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS `I was an overseas resident during that part`
            `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS
                `I was in Great Britain during that part` OR `the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` `I was in a part of the Channel Islands during that part` `given` `that part is subject to an Order under section 179`

-- Regulation 22 and 10. The increment for each whole week is the percentage of that weekly rate.
@export How much does each whole week of that part of my deferral add to my weekly pension, in pounds (reg 22)?
GIVEN `the weekly rate my increment is worked from` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate, in pounds, that your increment is worked from (see the previous question)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does each whole week of that part of my deferral add to my weekly pension` IS
    `the increment under regulation 22, the weekly rate being` `the weekly rate my increment is worked from`

-- Regulation 23. Where both regulation 12A (a change in my weekly rate other than by up-rating) and regulation 22 apply, the increment is worked out under 22 and then adjusted as
-- 12A directs; as the text is written the adjustment is nil (see NOTES.md, fork F20).
@export How much does each whole week add to my weekly pension where regulations 12A and 22 both apply, in pounds (reg 23)?
GIVEN `the weekly rate my increment is worked from` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate, in pounds, that regulation 22 says your increment is worked from?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does each whole week add to my weekly pension where regulations 12A and 22 both apply` IS
    `the increment under regulation 23, the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to being` `the weekly rate my increment is worked from`

§§ `National Insurance credits that count towards my State Pension (Part 8) -- only if you are asking whether a particular week is credited`

-- Regulation 25(3). A week is named by its first day. A week that falls partly in one tax year (6 April to 5 April) and partly in the next falls in the year it begins in.
@export In which tax year does a week count (reg 25(3))?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `In which tax year does a week count` IS
    `the tax year a week falls in` `the first day of my week`

-- Regulation 24(2). Nothing in Chapter 3 credits you for a day, or an event, before 6 April 2016, so a week that begins before then is out of Chapter 3.
@export Can I be credited for a week under Chapter 3 of the Regulations (reg 24(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be credited for a week under Chapter 3 of the Regulations` IF
    `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of my week`

-- Regulation 25(2). Where you would be credited with earnings or contributions for a year or a week, you are credited only to the extent necessary to make the year a qualifying year.
@export How much will I actually be credited with, limited to what my year needs (reg 25(2))?
GIVEN `what I would be credited with` IS A NUMBER @desc How much would you be credited with for the year or week, apart from this limit?
      `what my year still needs to be a qualifying year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does the year still need to be a qualifying year? (0 if it already is one.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will I actually be credited with` IS
    `the amount the person is credited with` `what I would be credited with` `limited by` `what my year still needs to be a qualifying year`

-- Regulations 26 and 27. For a year before 6 April 2016, you are credited with what you would have been entitled to under the 1975 Regulations (regulation 26) or section 23A of the
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (regulation 27, a Class 3 contribution for parents and carers) for a Category A retirement pension, had the 2014 Act amendment
-- not come into force and you attained pensionable age on 6 April 2016. That entitlement is stated by you.
@export Am I credited for a week before 6 April 2016 as if I had reached pension age on that day (reg 26)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `I would have been entitled to the credit on those assumptions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to the credit under the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975 for a Category A retirement pension, had the amendment of the 2014 Act not come into force and had you attained pensionable age on 6 April 2016?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited for a week before 6 April 2016 as if I had reached pension age on that day` IF
    `the person is credited under regulation 26` `the first day of my week` `given` `I would have been entitled to the credit on those assumptions`

@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week before 6 April 2016 as a parent or carer (reg 27)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `I would have been entitled to the contribution on those assumptions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to a Class 3 contribution under section 23A of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (or regulations made under it) for a Category A retirement pension, had the 2014 Act amendment not come into force and had you attained pensionable age on 6 April 2016?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week before 6 April 2016 as a parent or carer` IF
    `the person is credited under regulation 27` `the first day of my week` `given` `I would have been entitled to the contribution on those assumptions`

-- Regulation 28. A spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, is credited with a Class 3 contribution
-- for a week in a year from 6 April 1975 to 5 April 2016 in which the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor, but only if they apply, for a past period, in the
-- form and with the information the Secretary of State requires. The application is what you owe; the week and the factors are the facts.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces, for a week before 6 April 2016 (reg 28)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `I am a spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or treated as one by the Secretary of State for occupying accommodation?
      `I am accompanying the member outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or treated by the Secretary of State as doing so?
      `the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that year, do the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor?
      `I am entitled to a credit that week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled that week to be credited under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman whose reduced rate election under section 19(4) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 is in force in any part of that week?
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received your application to be credited?
      `the day the Secretary of State received my application` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if none.)
      `my application is on an approved form or accepted as sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient?
      `my application includes the information required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the information specified by the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces for a week before 6 April 2016` IF
    `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` `my forces spouse facts`
    WHERE
        `my forces spouse facts` MEANS `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` WITH
            `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS `I am a spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
            `the person is accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS `I am accompanying the member outside the United Kingdom`
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of my week`
            `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS `the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor`
            `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS `I am entitled to a credit that week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations`
            `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force`
            `the date the Secretary of State receives the application` IS
                IF `I have applied` THEN JUST `the day the Secretary of State received my application` ELSE NOTHING
            `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances` IS `my application is on an approved form or accepted as sufficient`
            `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS `my application includes the information required`

-- Regulation 33. The same as regulation 28 for a week in a year beginning on or after 6 April 2016 (the conditions, exclusions and application are the same words).
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces, for a week from 6 April 2016 (reg 33)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `I am a spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or treated as one by the Secretary of State for occupying accommodation?
      `I am accompanying the member outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or treated by the Secretary of State as doing so?
      `the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that year, do the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor?
      `I am entitled to a credit that week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled that week to be credited under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman whose reduced rate election under section 19(4) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 is in force in any part of that week?
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received your application to be credited?
      `the day the Secretary of State received my application` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if none.)
      `my application is on an approved form or accepted as sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient?
      `my application includes the information required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the information specified by the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces for a week from 6 April 2016` IF
    `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` `my forces spouse facts`
    WHERE
        `my forces spouse facts` MEANS `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` WITH
            `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS `I am a spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
            `the person is accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS `I am accompanying the member outside the United Kingdom`
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of my week`
            `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS `the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor`
            `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS `I am entitled to a credit that week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations`
            `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force`
            `the date the Secretary of State receives the application` IS
                IF `I have applied` THEN JUST `the day the Secretary of State received my application` ELSE NOTHING
            `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances` IS `my application is on an approved form or accepted as sufficient`
            `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS `my application includes the information required`

-- Regulation 29. A credit you receive under one of nine provisions of the 1975 Regulations (approved training; carer's allowance or carer support payment; disability element of working
-- tax credit; unemployment; incapacity for work or limited capability for work; jury service; maternity pay; certain imprisonment or detention; certain spouses and civil partners of
-- members of the forces) also counts for the 2014 Act. That you were credited under it is the other side's fact, which you state.
@export Does a credit I received under the 1975 Regulations also count for my State Pension (reg 29)?
GIVEN `the provision I was credited under` IS A `Provision of the 1975 Regulations` @desc Under which provision of the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975 were you credited?
      `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you were credited for?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a credit I received under the 1975 Regulations also count for my State Pension` IF
    `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `the provision I was credited under` `for the week beginning` `the first day of my week`

-- Regulation 30. If you are paid working tax credit for a week in which you are an employed earner, or a self-employed earner with profits below the small profits threshold, or
-- excepted by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001, you are credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit; unless you are entitled that week to a
-- credit under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations, or are a woman with a reduced rate election in force. Where the credit is paid for a couple, it is the member
-- assessed as having earnings (or, if both are assessed, the member it is paid to). Whom the credit is paid to is the State's side.
@export What earnings am I credited with for a week in which I am paid working tax credit, in pounds (reg 30)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `working tax credit is paid for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is working tax credit paid to you (or for your couple) in respect of the week?
      `I am an employed earner that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employed earner that week?
      `I am a self-employed earner with small profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold, who would otherwise be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution?
      `I am excepted by regulation 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you excepted from being treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001?
      `it is paid for a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the working tax credit paid in respect of a couple?
      `only one of us has earnings assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is only one member of the couple assessed as having income consisting of earnings?
      `I am the member assessed as having earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you that member?
      `the earnings of each of us are assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are the earnings of each member of the couple assessed?
      `it is paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the working tax credit paid to you?
      `I am entitled to a credit that week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled that week to be credited under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman whose reduced rate election under section 19(4) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 is in force in any part of that week?
      `the lower earnings limit for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit in force for that week, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What earnings am I credited with for a week in which I am paid working tax credit` IS
    `the earnings credited under regulation 30` `my tax credit facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of my week`
    WHERE
        `my tax credit facts` MEANS `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid` WITH
            `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS `working tax credit is paid for the week`
            `the person is an employed earner in the week` IS `I am an employed earner that week`
            `the person is a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold, who would otherwise be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution` IS `I am a self-employed earner with small profits`
            `the person is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` IS `I am excepted by regulation 43`
            `the working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS `it is paid for a couple`
            `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS `only one of us has earnings assessed`
            `the person is the member assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS `I am the member assessed as having earnings`
            `the earnings of each member of the couple are assessed` IS `the earnings of each of us are assessed`
            `the working tax credit is paid to the person` IS `it is paid to me`
            `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS `I am entitled to a credit that week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B`
            `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force`
            `the lower earnings limit in force for the week` IS `the lower earnings limit for the week`

-- Regulation 31. You are credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week for any part of which you are entitled to universal credit.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I am entitled to universal credit (reg 31)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `I am entitled to universal credit for part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 for any part of the week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I am entitled to universal credit` IF
    `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 31` `the first day of my week` `given` `I am entitled to universal credit for part of the week`

-- Regulation 32. A man born before 6 October 1953 is credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit for each week in the year in which he attains the pensionable age of a woman
-- born the same day, and each later year before the one in which he attains 65, except a year in which he is absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days; and a self-employed man only if
-- he would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for small profits, or is excepted by regulation 43.
@export What earnings am I credited with as a man approaching pensionable age, in pounds (reg 32)?
GIVEN `I am a man` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a man?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I attain the pension age of a woman born on my birthday` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on the same day as you?
      `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `the days I was absent from Great Britain in that year` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in that tax year were you absent from Great Britain?
      `I am a self-employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed earner?
      `I would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for small profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, would you be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for your profits being below the small profits threshold?
      `I am excepted by regulation 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you excepted from being treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001?
      `the lower earnings limit for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit in force for that week, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What earnings am I credited with as a man approaching pensionable age` IS
    `the earnings credited under regulation 32` `my approaching-pensionable-age facts`
    WHERE
        `my approaching-pensionable-age facts` MEANS `Facts for a man approaching pensionable age` WITH
            `the person is a man` IS `I am a man`
            `the man's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day` IS `the day I attain the pension age of a woman born on my birthday`
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of my week`
            `the number of days in the year of the week that the man was absent from Great Britain` IS `the days I was absent from Great Britain in that year`
            `the man is a self-employed earner` IS `I am a self-employed earner`
            `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for profits below the small profits threshold` IS `I would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for small profits`
            `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` IS `I am excepted by regulation 43`
            `the lower earnings limit in force for the week` IS `the lower earnings limit for the week`

-- Regulation 34. You are credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which you are awarded child benefit for any part of it for a child under 12; or, as the partner of the person awarded
-- it, if you live with them, share responsibility for the child, are ordinarily resident in Great Britain, are not in custody, and apply to HM Revenue and Customs in time (regulation 39), for a
-- year in which their earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor. The award and their earnings factors are the other side's facts.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which child benefit is awarded (reg 34)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `child benefit is awarded to me for part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is child benefit awarded to you for any part of the week, in respect of a child under 12?
      `I am the partner of the person awarded child benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the partner of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week?
      `I live with that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, do you live with that person?
      `I share responsibility for the child with that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you share responsibility for the child with that person?
      `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in Great Britain?
      `I am not in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody?
      `I have applied to HM Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to HM Revenue and Customs to be credited?
      `the day HM Revenue and Customs received my application` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did they receive it? (Any date if none.)
      `HM Revenue and Customs consider further time reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was late: do the Commissioners consider it reasonable in the circumstances to allow further time?
      `their earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that year, do the earnings factors of the person awarded child benefit (leaving out credits derived from the award) exceed the qualifying earnings factor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which child benefit is awarded` IF
    `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` `my child benefit facts`
    WHERE
        `my child benefit facts` MEANS `Facts for credit in respect of child benefit` WITH
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of my week`
            `child benefit is awarded to the person for any part of the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS `child benefit is awarded to me for part of the week`
            `the person is the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week` IS `I am the partner of the person awarded child benefit`
            `the partner resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded` IS `I live with that person`
            `the partner shares responsibility for the child with that person` IS `I share responsibility for the child with that person`
            `the partner is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
            `the partner is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS `I am not in custody`
            `the partner has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS
                IF   `I have applied to HM Revenue and Customs`
                THEN JUST (`An application for a credit` WITH
                         `the date the application is received` IS `the day HM Revenue and Customs received my application`
                         `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances` IS `HM Revenue and Customs consider further time reasonable`)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the year exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS `their earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor`

-- Regulation 35. If you provided care for a child under 12, as one of the relatives or partners listed in paragraph (6) and ordinarily resident in Great Britain, and child benefit was awarded to
-- another person (whose earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor) for the child and the week, you are credited with a Class 3 contribution if you apply (with the
-- name and date of birth of each child, a declaration by that other person if one was requested, and the weeks) after the end of the year the week is in. If more than one person could be
-- credited, those persons elect, with that other person's agreement, which of them is credited; failing agreement it is for the Secretary of State to decide.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I cared for a child under 12 (reg 35)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `I provided care for a child under 12 that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide care in the week in respect of a child under 12?
      `my relationship to the child` IS A `Relationship to the child cared for` @desc What is your relationship to the child? (A sibling includes a half-blood, step or adopted sibling; a partner is the other member of a couple who live together as if married or civil partners without being so.)
      `I was ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you ordinarily resident in Great Britain that week?
      `child benefit was awarded to another person for the child and the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was child benefit awarded to another person in respect of the child (or each child) and that week?
      `that person's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that year, do that person's earnings factors (leaving out any regulation 34 credit) exceed the qualifying earnings factor?
      `I have applied to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to the Secretary of State to be credited?
      `the day the Secretary of State received my application` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did the Secretary of State receive it? (Any date if none.)
      `my application gives the name and date of birth of each child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include the name and date of birth of each child cared for?
      `a declaration by that other person was requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs ask for a declaration by that other person that the conditions are satisfied?
      `my application includes that declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does your application include it?
      `my application gives the weeks I cared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application specify the week or weeks in which each child was cared for?
      `more than one person could be credited for my week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could more than one person be credited for that week for caring for the child?
      `we have elected which of us is credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have those persons elected, with the other person's agreement, which of them is credited?
      `I am the one elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you the one elected?
GIVETH A `Whether a credit is given`
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I cared for a child under 12` IS
    `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` `my caring facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of my week`
    WHERE
        `my caring facts` MEANS `Facts for credit for caring for a child under 12` WITH
            `the person provided care in the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS `I provided care for a child under 12 that week`
            `the person's relationship to the child` IS `my relationship to the child`
            `the person was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS `I was ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
            `child benefit was awarded to another person in respect of the child, or each child, and the week` IS `child benefit was awarded to another person for the child and the week`
            `that other person's earnings factors, other than those derived from a regulation 34 credit, exceed the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS `that person's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor`
            `the person has applied to the Secretary of State` IS
                IF   `I have applied to the Secretary of State`
                THEN JUST (`An application for a credit` WITH
                         `the date the application is received` IS `the day the Secretary of State received my application`
                         -- Placeholder: regulation 39(b) gives no further time, so the rule called does not read this field.
                         `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances` IS FALSE)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `the application includes the name and date of birth of each child cared for` IS `my application gives the name and date of birth of each child`
            `the Secretary of State or the Commissioners requested a declaration by the other person` IS `a declaration by that other person was requested`
            `the application includes a declaration by the other person that the conditions in regulation 35(2) are satisfied` IS `my application includes that declaration`
            `the application specifies the week or weeks in which each child was cared for` IS `my application gives the weeks I cared`
            `more than one person could be credited for the week` IS `more than one person could be credited for my week`
            `those persons have elected, with the agreement of the other person, which of them is to be credited` IS `we have elected which of us is credited`
            `this person is the one elected` IS `I am the one elected`

-- Regulation 36. A foster parent (approved under one of four regimes), ordinarily resident in Great Britain and not in custody, is credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week if they
-- apply to HM Revenue and Customs in time (regulation 39).
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I am a foster parent (reg 36)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `how I am approved as a foster parent` IS A `Approval as a foster parent` @desc Under which provision are you approved as a foster parent, kinship carer or foster carer (or none of them)?
      `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in Great Britain?
      `I am not in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody?
      `I have applied to HM Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to HM Revenue and Customs to be credited?
      `the day HM Revenue and Customs received my application` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did they receive it? (Any date if none.)
      `HM Revenue and Customs consider further time reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was late: do the Commissioners consider it reasonable in the circumstances to allow further time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I am a foster parent` IF
    `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` `my foster parent facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of my week`
    WHERE
        `my foster parent facts` MEANS `Facts for credit as a foster parent` WITH
            `the person's approval` IS `how I am approved as a foster parent`
            `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
            `the person is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS `I am not in custody`
            `the person has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS
                IF   `I have applied to HM Revenue and Customs`
                THEN JUST (`An application for a credit` WITH
                         `the date the application is received` IS `the day HM Revenue and Customs received my application`
                         `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances` IS `HM Revenue and Customs consider further time reasonable`)
                ELSE NOTHING

-- Regulation 37. You are credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which you are engaged in caring: caring for 20 or more hours for people each entitled to a relevant benefit (or
-- where the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate), or a person to whom paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies; not
-- while you are not ordinarily resident in Great Britain or in custody. For caring for 20 or more hours you must apply (a declaration of the hours, the name and number of each person cared for,
-- the relevant benefit, and a declaration by an appropriate person if asked) in time (regulation 39), except that a woman with a reduced rate election in force need not (see NOTES.md, fork F25).
-- At most two persons cared for can be asked about; the longer encoding takes any number.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I care for someone (reg 37)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `the hours I cared that week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many hours in the week did you care for another person or persons?
      `the benefit of the first person I care for` IS A `Relevant benefit` @desc Which relevant benefit is the first person you care for entitled to for the week (or none)?
      `I care for a second person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you care for a second person?
      `the benefit of the second person I care for` IS A `Relevant benefit` @desc If so, which relevant benefit is that person entitled to for the week (or none)? (Any if none.)
      `the Secretary of State thinks that level of care is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that level of care appropriate?
      `I am within paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 apply to you?
      `I was ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you ordinarily resident in Great Britain that week?
      `I was in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody that week?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman whose reduced rate election under section 19(4) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 is in force in any part of that week?
      `I have applied to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to the Secretary of State to be credited?
      `the day the Secretary of State received my application` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did the Secretary of State receive it? (Any date if none.)
      `the Secretary of State considers further time reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was late: does the Secretary of State consider it reasonable in the circumstances to allow further time?
      `my application declares 20 or more hours a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include your declaration that you care for 20 or more hours in a week?
      `my application names each person I care for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for?
      `my application says which relevant benefit each is entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say, where applicable, which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to?
      `a declaration by an appropriate person was requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State ask for a declaration by an appropriate person as to the level of care?
      `my application includes that declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does your application include a declaration signed by an appropriate person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in which I care for someone` IF
    `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` `my caring-for-someone facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of my week`
    WHERE
        `my caring-for-someone facts` MEANS `Facts for credit for caring` WITH
            `the hours the person cared for another person or persons in the week` IS `the hours I cared that week`
            `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week` IS
                IF   `I care for a second person`
                THEN LIST `the benefit of the first person I care for`, `the benefit of the second person I care for`
                ELSE LIST `the benefit of the first person I care for`
            `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS `the Secretary of State thinks that level of care is appropriate`
            `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person` IS `I am within paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B`
            `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS `I was ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
            `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody in the week` IS `I was in custody`
            `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force`
            `the person has applied to the Secretary of State` IS
                IF   `I have applied to the Secretary of State`
                THEN JUST (`An application for a credit` WITH
                         `the date the application is received` IS `the day the Secretary of State received my application`
                         `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances` IS `the Secretary of State considers further time reasonable`)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `the application includes a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for 20 or more hours in a week` IS `my application declares 20 or more hours a week`
            `the application includes the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for` IS `my application names each person I care for`
            `the application says, where applicable, which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to` IS `my application says which relevant benefit each is entitled to`
            `the Secretary of State requested a declaration by an appropriate person as to the level of care` IS `a declaration by an appropriate person was requested`
            `the application includes a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care` IS `my application includes that declaration`

-- Regulation 38. You are credited with a Class 3 contribution for twelve weeks before you become entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support, for
-- twelve weeks after the week in which your entitlement to it ends (but not in a week in which you are credited under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations because of it), and for twelve
-- weeks after a week in which you stop satisfying regulation 37(2)(a).
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in the twelve weeks around carer's allowance or caring (reg 38)?
GIVEN `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week?
      `which twelve weeks I am asking about` IS A `Circumstance of an additional period of credit` @desc Is the week in the twelve weeks before you became entitled to carer's allowance (or carer support payment), after you ceased to be entitled, or after a week in which you stopped satisfying regulation 37(2)(a)?
      `the day my entitlement began or the first day of the week it ended` IS A DATE @desc For the first, the day your entitlement began; for the others, the first day of the week in which your entitlement ended or you stopped satisfying regulation 37(2)(a).
      `I am credited that week under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations because of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled that week under regulation 7A of the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975 to be credited because of carer's allowance or carer support payment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for a week in the twelve weeks around carer's allowance or caring` IF
    `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` `my additional period facts`
    WHERE
        `my additional period facts` MEANS `Facts for an additional period of credit` WITH
            `the circumstance` IS `which twelve weeks I am asking about`
            `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends` IS `the day my entitlement began or the first day of the week it ended`
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of my week`
            `the person is entitled in the week under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations to be credited because of carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` IS `I am credited that week under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations because of it`

-- Regulation 39. An application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37 must be received before the end of the year after the one the week is in, or within further time the Secretary of State or
-- the Commissioners consider reasonable; an application under regulation 35 must be received after the end of the year the week is in. This is what you owe: the application, in time.
@export Is my application for a credit in time (reg 39)?
GIVEN `which application I am making` IS A `Kind of application under regulation 39` @desc Which application are you making?
      `the first day of my week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are applying for?
      `the day my application is received` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your application received?
      `further time is considered reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is late: does the Secretary of State (or the Commissioners, as the case may be) consider it reasonable in the circumstances to allow further time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application for a credit in time` IF
    `the application is received in time` `which application I am making` `for the week beginning` `the first day of my week` `and the application being` `my application`
    WHERE
        `my application` MEANS `An application for a credit` WITH
            `the date the application is received` IS `the day my application is received`
            `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances` IS `further time is considered reasonable`
